# Automated PR Review Gate (Pre-Merge)

Merge to `main` only when the **dual gate** holds on the same latest head SHA:
**required CI is green** and **review quiescence** (including the arrival wait).
Neither half is enough. Human modus operandi: `docs/pr-merge-gate.md`.

**Workflow detail:** `@.cursor/rules/013-pr-review-correction-loop.mdc`.

## Bots / sources in scope

Address findings from **all** of these when present:

- **CodeRabbit** (`coderabbitai`) — real `APPROVED` / `COMMENTED` review on the latest head (not a rate-limit placeholder), except the bounded fallbacks in step 6.
- **CodeAnt** (`codeant-ai`) — inline suggestions + quality gates. “🔄 Reviewing your PR…” is in-progress, not quiescence.
- **Sourcery** (`sourcery-ai`) — inline `suggestion` / `nitpick` / `suggestion (bug_risk)`. `bug_risk` is a correctness bug. Do **not** `@sourcery-ai review` while the 250k / 7-day budget is exhausted. Auto “Reviewer’s Guide” is not a real review.
- **GitHub Copilot** (`copilot-pull-request-reviewer`)
- **DeepSource** (`deepsource-io`) — **always** comment `@deepsourcebot review` (first line exact) after opening a PR and after every fix push. Static analysis alone is not enough. Dashboard JavaScript analyzer remains off.
- **CodeScene** — address actionable comments when the check runs.
- Other automated reviewers when present (Socket when blocking, Cursor Bugbot when requested, Greptile / Codex — skip and document if trial/budget returns no review).

Human review comments that request concrete fixes are in scope while open.

## Scope (mandatory)

Address **every** item: critical / high / medium, **nitpicks**, **outside-of-diff-range** comments, suggestions, refactors, and doc notes.

## Workflow (loop until clear)

1. After pushing, trigger: **always** `@deepsourcebot review`; `@coderabbitai review` when a full review is missing/stale/rate-limited; `@sourcery-ai review` only when Sourcery has not reviewed the latest head **and** the 250k / 7-day budget is not exhausted.
2. Collect all review threads **and** every review body on the current head (outside-diff items live only in the body). Wait for in-progress bots to **arrive** (arrival wait — PR #299).
3. Fix or reply with a documented English rationale (rare — prefer fixing).
4. Push follow-ups; re-trigger DeepSource and CodeRabbit; **repeat until no new actionable comments remain**.
5. Do **not** merge while unresolved comments remain, a bot is still “Reviewing”, or required CI is red.

## CodeRabbit rate-limit loop (mandatory — never skip)

A green CodeRabbit check that only says **“Review rate limited”** is **not** a completed review.

1. Parse **`Next review available in: N minutes`**.
2. **Wait** at least `N` minutes (+ 2–5 minutes buffer). Typical windows: 14–60+ minutes.
3. Re-poll issue comments + `pulls/N/reviews` for `coderabbitai[bot]` on the **current** head SHA.
4. Post a clean top-level `@coderabbitai review`.
5. If still rate-limited, repeat up to **3** wait/re-trigger cycles on the same head (document each attempt).
6. **After 3 failed wait/re-trigger cycles, or a single wait exceeding 90 minutes, with no real CodeRabbit review yet posted for the current head** — this exact threshold, repeated verbatim in `013`, `docs/pr-merge-gate.md`, and `docs/ci-branch-governance.md` — CodeRabbit becomes **optional as a blocker**, via **one** of:
   - **(b) Sourcery stand-in** (maintainer-approved 2026-08-05): Sourcery has a real, non-rate-limited review on the current head with all actionable findings resolved, and no other in-scope bot has an unresolved item or active `CHANGES_REQUESTED`.
   - **(c) 2026-09-03 skip** (standing policy): Sourcery **cannot** stand in (budget exhausted, or no real Sourcery review is available), **and** the wait loop has been run **or** a CodeRabbit UI hang on this head is documented in a PR comment, **and** at least one other in-scope bot has a real review on the current head with everything resolved, **and** no in-progress late-bot wave remains.
   Post a disposition comment (timestamps, cycles, who is standing in). These fallbacks apply **only** while CodeRabbit has produced no real review of the current head. A `CHANGES_REQUESTED` CodeRabbit review on the **latest** head is **never** waived.
7. **Single exact quiescence predicate** (this is the one authoritative rule — `013`, `docs/pr-merge-gate.md`, and `docs/ci-branch-governance.md` restate it, they do not vary it). **“Latest head” / “current head”** is the PR’s current head SHA. Quiescence requires **all** of the following:
   - **Dual gate — CI half:** required blocking CI is green on the latest head (`docs/ci-branch-governance.md`).
   - **Primary CodeRabbit condition:** **(a)** a real, **non-`CHANGES_REQUESTED`** CodeRabbit review (`APPROVED` or `COMMENTED`, body proves it isn’t a rate-limit placeholder) targeting the latest head; **or (b)** the Sourcery stand-in in step 6; **or (c)** the 2026-09-03 skip in step 6.
   - **`@deepsourcebot review` has been attempted on the current head** (recorded attempt — static analysis alone does not satisfy this).
   - **No active human `CHANGES_REQUESTED` review targets the current head** (moot once superseded by a later non-requesting human review or explicit approval).
   - **Arrival wait is complete:** no in-scope bot is still in-progress on the current head (CodeAnt “🔄 Reviewing…”, pending Greptile / Copilot / CodeScene / CodeRabbit). GraphQL `reviewThreads` = 0 is necessary but not sufficient if a bot has not finished arriving.
   - **No other in-scope bot has an unresolved item or active `CHANGES_REQUESTED`.**
   - **All actionable GraphQL threads are resolved**, and **every body-only finding** (outside-diff comments, human top-level review bodies, or any finding with no thread ID) **has a recorded `fixed`, `replied`, or `deferred` disposition** in the disposition ledger or a PR comment, with a documented English rationale for every `deferred` finding.

   A `CHANGES_REQUESTED` review (bot or human) **never** satisfies quiescence by itself. After fixing, wait for a non-requesting review on a **later** head — thread resolution alone does not moot it. A `CHANGES_REQUESTED` review on a **superseded** commit is not a merge block once a newer real review exists for the current head.

## Exceptions

- Duplicate comments already fixed in a later commit: mark resolved and cite the commit.
- False positives: short English reply explaining why + resolve thread after confirmation.

See `docs/pr-merge-gate.md` and English content policy `@.cursor/rules/010-english-content.mdc`.

<example>

CodeRabbit shows "Review rate limited" on the current head. Parse the wait time, wait it out (+buffer), re-trigger `@coderabbitai review`, and repeat up to 3 cycles / 90 minutes. A real `APPROVED`/`COMMENTED` review lands on cycle 2 — all inline threads it raised are fixed and resolved, and its one body-only "outside diff range" finding is fixed and recorded as `fixed` in the PR disposition comment. Arrival wait is complete and required CI is green — then merge.

</example>

<example type="invalid">

Required CI is green and GraphQL `reviewThreads` returns 0. Merge immediately while CodeAnt still shows “🔄 Reviewing your PR…” and Greptile has not posted — the arrival wait never completed (PR #299 miss).

</example>
